  "response": "## What the finding points at\n\n`crime_00064` — **Duplicate Component Shape**, medium / confidence 0.70:\n\n```\nshape: <div> subtree, hash e96b55b64336…   4 file(s), 4 occurrence(s)\ndashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:142-150\ndashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:152-160\ndashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:101-109\ndashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:112-120\n```\n\nReading those line ranges, the repeated subtree is the **form action bar** — the footer that closes every invoice form:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link href=\"/dashboard/invoices\" className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\">\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nAll four copies are byte-identical except the submit label (`Create Invoice` / `Edit Invoice`). The cancel href, the six-class hover/transition recipe, the `h-10`, the `gap-4` — all hand-copied. That's the drift surface: change the cancel style or add a pending state and you have four edits, and nothing fails if you only make three.\n\n## Constraint worth naming up front\n\n`final-example/` and `starter-example/` are **two independent Next apps** — separate `package.json`, separate `tsconfig.json`, each mapping `@/*` → `./*`. There is no module graph edge between them, so one component cannot serve all four call sites without introducing a workspace package (`packages/ui`) and rewiring both apps' builds. That's a bigger change than this finding warrants.\n\nSo the proposal is **one component per app, two call sites each** — which kills the drift where it actually matters (create vs. edit within an app, the pair that genuinely diverges). I note the cross-app half below as a deliberate non-fix.\n\n## Shared component\n\n**Name:** `InvoiceFormActions`\n**Location:** `app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` (one per app)\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport function InvoiceFormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  children,\n}: {\n  cancelHref: string;\n  submitLabel: string;\n  cancelLabel?: string;\n  children?: ReactNode;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\">{submitLabel}</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Public API\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cancelHref` | `string` | — required | Today always `/dashboard/invoices`, but a customer form would differ. Required, not defaulted, so a new call site has to state its escape route rather than silently inherit the invoices list. |\n| `submitLabel` | `string` | — required | The only thing that actually varies across the four copies. |\n| `cancelLabel` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Cheap; covers \"Discard\" / \"Back\" without a fork. |\n| `children` | `ReactNode` | — | **Slot.** Leading actions, rendered left of Cancel — the natural home for a destructive `Delete invoice` on the edit form. Without it, edit-form re-forks the wrapper the first time it needs a third button. |\n\n**Deliberately not props:**\n\n- **`className`** — an escape hatch here re-opens the exact drift the component closes. If a call site needs different spacing, that's a second variant, decided explicitly.\n- **A `submit` ReactNode override** — `submitLabel` covers all four sites. Adding a full slot now invites call sites to pass their own `<Button>` and lose the shared `type=\"submit\"`.\n- **`pending` / `disabled`** — none of the four call sites tracks it today. Add it when a call site needs it; the prop is trivial to introduce and the `Button` already accepts the pass-through.\n\n**Server/client:** no hooks, no handlers — leave `'use client'` off. That matters: `starter-example/create-form.tsx` is currently a server component (no `'use client'`), while the other three are client components. A directive-free `InvoiceFormActions` imports cleanly into both.\n\n## Files that change\n\n**final-example** (2 edits + 1 new)\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` | **new** — component above |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | L142–150 → `<InvoiceFormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />`; drop the now-unused `Link` and `Button` imports (L4, L11) |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | L152–160 → same with `submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\"`; drop `Link` / `Button` imports (L10, L11) |\n\n**starter-example** (2 edits + 1 new)\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` | **new** — identical component |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | L101–109 → `submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\"`; drop `Link` / `Button` imports (L2, L9) |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | L112–120 → `submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\"`; drop `Link` / `Button` imports (L10, L11) |\n\nNet: 6 files, ~36 duplicated JSX lines collapse to 4 call sites plus two ~24-line components. Verify by re-running `crimes scan --format json` — `crime_00064` should drop out (the four occurrences fall below the detector's threshold).\n\n## What this leaves on the table\n\nThree things I did **not** fold in, since they're outside what the finding names:\n\n1. **The form bodies are near-duplicates too.** Customer select, amount input, and the status fieldset are ~85 lines repeated across the same four files, varying only by `defaultValue`/`defaultChecked`. The detector flagged the footer because it's the largest *exactly*-matching subtree; the bigger consolidation is `<InvoiceFields invoice?={...} customers={...} />`. That's a real refactor with real risk (the `aria-describedby` error wiring exists in final-example but not starter-example), not a mechanical extraction.\n2. **Cross-app sharing** — needs a `packages/ui` workspace and build changes in both apps, as above.\n3. **`crime_00065` / `crime_00066`** flag `invoice.status === 'pending'` / `'paid'` scattered across edit-form and status.tsx. If the status fieldset ever gets extracted, that's the moment to route those through one policy helper rather than duplicating the comparisons into the new component.",
